  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Source and generation ownership",
      "items": [
        "Brief: the server derives its entire source manifest from the record watermark; deterministic composition creates cited facts, gaps and contradictions.",
        "Reports/explanations: the requester selects a bounded source subset; relevant exclusions carry reasons. An explanation is separately authored and reviewed; a report does not automatically become one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Validation and visibility gates",
      "items": [
        "Mechanical flags block validation until corrected or dispositioned with a reason; a mechanical pass does not prove clinical support. A human inspects the cited revision and qualifier.",
        "A successful task creates only a draft candidate. Recheck current access, lease, target version and freshness before committing; late/cancelled results preserve human edits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Independent histories",
      "items": [
        "Source corrections append a new revision; relevant changes mark content STALE and keep reviewed text/history. Regeneration creates a candidate/new draft.",
        "Publication replacement is atomic and guarded by current versions; withdrawal blocks future reads/downloads. Already downloaded copies cannot be recalled. Each attachment needs its own explicit grant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Other state axes and delivery scope",
      "items": [
        "Appointment BOOKED/CHECKED_IN/COMPLETED/CANCELLED/NO_SHOW is separate from consultation IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED/CANCELLED. Task QUEUED/RUNNING/SUCCEEDED/FAILED/CANCELLED is separate from review and CURRENT/STALE.",
        "P-03 patient explanation export is in increment 1. P-01 clinician brief and P-02 report follow in increment 2; clinician-only exports remain clinician-only. PDFBox is the proposed renderer."
      ]
    }
  ]
